{"id":"neet-2025-q052","pn":52,"y":"NEET 2025","tp":"The p-Block Elements","st":"Group 15 hydrides and oxides","q":"Given below are two statements :\nStatement I : Like nitrogen that can form ammonia, arsenic can form arsine.\nStatement II : Antimony cannot form antimony pentoxide.\nIn the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below :","o":["Both Statement I and Statement II are correct","Both Statement I and Statement II are incorrect","Statement I is correct but Statement II is incorrect","Statement I is incorrect but Statement II is correct"],"c":2,"s":"All group 15 elements form hydrides of EH₃ type.\nNitrogen forms ammonia (NH₃) and arsenic forms arsine (AsH₃).\nAll group 15 elements form two types of oxides: E₂O₃ and E₂O₅.\nAntimony forms antimony pentoxide Sb₂O₅.\nSo Statement I is correct and Statement II is incorrect."}
